{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564024-charms-for-warding-against-quiet","id":1564024,"title":"Charms for warding against Quiet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-09-13T17:39:46-07:00","id":1564024,"title":"Charms for warding against Quiet","content":"I was reading <i>How do you DO that? </i>in order to see what spheres and levels of said spheres would be needed to craft a charm that would make the user not only capable of seeing and go against illusions made by other Mages, but also capable of identifying and unravel lies ingrained in the user's psyche (be it those lies told by others or the user themself). The more I was reflecting on this particular idea, I concluded that what I really thought about was essentially a charm that would defend the Mage against Quiet, or at least make it so it's easier to &quot;Rise Out of Quiet&quot; (for example, diminishing the difficulty of the tests).<br /> <br /> But then, I ran into some problems. First, the wards exemplified in the book are mainly around defending against external factors, not internal ones, which makes sense given that the sub-section explaining how to use wards makes part of the large chapter on Summoning. I went to the chapter focused mainly on Mind effects (<i>Uncanny Influence</i>) and although it gave me some ideas (mainly that such charm would need Conceptual Entropy i.e. Entropy 5), but again most of the scenarios of use in the chapter deal with an external force trying to influence you and not your own demons trying to wreak havoc in your mind. Lastly, I'm not even sure if such ward would be possible, given that the chapter on Summoning makes it quite clear that &quot;<i>wards cannot be set against Paradox</i>&quot;, which makes me think that it would also not help in dealing with Quiet.<br /> <br /> So... what to DO here (pun intended)? If such a charm is even possible to build with RAW, it would need obscenes amounts of Quintesscence (and Prime 4), at least Mind 4, Entropy 5. Maybe Life, since there are biological components that alter your mind state?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28986-agrat","name":"Agrat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28986_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T19:47:16-07:00","id":1564031,"title":"","content":"The first thing is to ignore that pike of garbage, HDYDT will require you have 3 Spheres at 4 to brew coffee if it can find anything argument for it.<br /> <br /> Now, you do have two different problems here, and understanding the distinction is essential, but also just how obscenely deep both are.<br /> <br /> 1. Protection against inner &quot;lies&quot;. That seems straightforward, but isn't. What is a lie? What is an ingrained one? How would you define the type of information you want the Magic to flag?<br /> <br /> A lie is a matter of perspective, and Mage is a game based on the whole reality being a matter of perspective. Magic is to Will your beliefs unto the world successfully. How can a Magic born of your Subjectivity understand an objective truth and force it over the Will that empowers it in the first place?<br /> <br /> Semantic details become very important here to analyze if this is actually a pretty simple and straightforward Effect, or actually the kind of fundamental question of Reality that can drive several chronicles.<br /> <br /> 2. Quiet is not about self-deception, even if the symptoms can include this, and crucially it is not about your mind. It's about your Magic.<br /> <br /> What sets Quiet apart from &quot;regular&quot; disorders a Mage is also prone to develop is that Quiet is a Magical phenomenon affecting your powers and how you relate to them. I personally find it easier as a Psychologist to explain Quiet as your Magic going insane rather than yourself.<br /> <br /> The symptoms then are following in reverse: it is not that delusions and hallucinations within your mind trickle into your powers, but rather that your Magic is going haywire, tainted by surges of power and Paradox and unbalanced Resonance, and it affects you and your mind like it affects the rest of the world. <hr /><br /> Understanding difference between symptom and cause here is also important, because without one expression the cause will find another. A person who thinks they're being surveiled by Martians don't have a problem because they believe that, they believe that because they have a problem.<br /> <br /> The delusion is not a conclusion, it is an expression that was put there for a reason, which is why they're so resistant to reasoning even if otherwise rational, and also means of you do manage to break through obstination and dissolve the delusion, the vulnerability the problem caused (not necessarily the problem itself) is exposed to a potential crisis while the mind finds another expression. You solved nothing.<br /> <br /> With Quiet this is even more marked because the whole mental breakdown doesn't really hold much of a key for the cause of the Quiet. Yes, it uses your psyche to give form to itself, and yes, your inner demons are very probably behind why you used your Magic the way you did. But a Quiet itself is a Magical phenomenon and not the madness' content, what solves it is to rebalance the foundations of Resonance. <hr /><br /> How can we actually try those things?<br /> <br /> The first will depend on what you call a lie to self and what kind of Truth you want to get out of it.<br /> <br /> For the Charm against Quiet, I'd say you can get some basic stuff with as low as Mind 1, Prime 1: an Effect that both observes your mental state in a general sense and your flow of Resonance, Paradox and Quintessence to verify the heavier imbalances.<br /> <br /> You can get a lot against Quiet simply out of knowing sooner you're in Quiet, or at imminent risk. In fact this woukd also be your best bet overall, as anything stringer would also ne veering closer to Paradox and the risk of being flipped by it from a protection against Quiet into an amplifier of Quiet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T07:54:46-07:00","id":1564040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564024-charms-for-warding-against-quiet?p=1564031#post1564031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first thing is to ignore that pike of garbage, HDYDT will require you have 3 Spheres at 4 to brew coffee if it can find anything argument for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if the author happens to dislike that brand of coffee, it will take six extra successes and a point of paradox for each minute you take to drink it.<br /> <br /> The wards section is one of the worst and I could dedicate an entire thread to breaking down how many places it contradicts the main rules, contradicts itself, or includes effects you don't need a Correspondence Ward for. That said...<br /> <br /> There is one ward in there that has some promise in this application. A mage can set up paradigmatic wards to block magic cast by certain mages. I don't remember what the alleged Sphere combination is nor would I trust HDYDT, but the point is that it is supposedly possible. From that we can also presume a mage can set up wards against the magic from certain resonances. Between those two, it should be possible to cobble together a ward against Hobgoblins.<br /> <br /> Now I don't actually remember if the magic of a Quiet counts as part of the Quiet-afflicted's paradigm, nor if it has the same resonance as the mage, but as long as the answer for either one is a clear yes or no it should be possible to, with effort, set up a ward to block out those manifestations. Either it does, and a ward blocks the mage's paradigm/resonance is the starting point, or it doesn't, and a ward blocks everything but his paradigm/resonance is the starting point.<br /> <br /> And this is a case where I'm glad there's not already a clear answer because this is the kind of story I wouldn't want to be easy. This is the kind of thing that should take research and effort and maybe a dash of desperation. That is, its not a quick fix, its a story idea.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T13:43:25-07:00","id":1564056,"title":"","content":"Basic question. The Quiet is a risk but that risk is based on the Mage trying to go beyond their limits or from the failure to face serious problems within themselves. Wouldn't eliminating the Quiet also tend to eliminate most or all personal growth?<br /> <br /> The Quiet and personal growth as a mage come from similar source, mainly the Avatar. Wouldn't the only way to seal of the Quiet be to cease being a Mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T00:59:01-07:00","id":1564071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564024-charms-for-warding-against-quiet?p=1564056#post1564056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basic question. The Quiet is a risk but that risk is based on the Mage trying to go beyond their limits or from the failure to face serious problems within themselves. Wouldn't eliminating the Quiet also tend to eliminate most or all personal growth?<br /> <br /> The Quiet and personal growth as a mage come from similar source, mainly the Avatar. Wouldn't the only way to seal of the Quiet be to cease being a Mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly, but that's beyond the scope here. What they asked for was a charm to help against it, not a seal to eliminate it.<br /> <br /> And neither the Quiet or the personal growth come from the Avatar. We don't know where any of them come from or the nature of their relationship, but we do know Mages existed before Avatars as we understand them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T13:24:53-07:00","id":1564095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564024-charms-for-warding-against-quiet?p=1564031#post1564031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What sets Quiet apart from &quot;regular&quot; disorders a Mage is also prone to develop is that Quiet is a Magical phenomenon affecting your powers and how you relate to them. I personally find it easier as a Psychologist to explain Quiet as your Magic going insane rather than yourself.<br /> <br /> The symptoms then are following in reverse: it is not that delusions and hallucinations within your mind trickle into your powers, but rather that your Magic is going haywire, tainted by surges of power and Paradox and unbalanced Resonance, and it affects you and your mind like it affects the rest of the world. <hr /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is a really good description and it pairs well with one other aspect of Quiet that I keep struggling to put into words, which is that there is a break between perception and reality but that break happens outside the mage, before reality reaches his senses. The magic often isn't altering the mage's mind in any direct way, it is affecting the experiences his mind receives and processes.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a horror short story I once read with one simple premise. The main character has a device that he can use to erase his own painful memories. He starts by only erasing his most painful ones, but then the worst of what is left become his most painful ones. Soon he is erasing embarrassments and social faux pas. Only now, he\u2019s missing so much information and experience that he frequently has awkward moments where he gets caught not knowing things he should\u2026 and he erases those moments too.<br /> <br /> In the story we meet him at a point where this has been going on for a very long time, and he now has so little experience at dealing with awkwardness and embarrassment that he\u2019s actually getting violent when those moments happen. In an expected horror story turn, he kills someone, and the indication is this isn\u2019t the first time though he certainly doesn\u2019t remember any others. Nor will he remember this time.<br /> <br /> Now I have no idea if this scenario would actually lead someone to violence and that's not why I brought it up, but the story illustrates the idea. The problem doesn\u2019t lie within the main character\u2019s mind, it lies with what reaches it and what gets to stay. His mind is processing as well as it can, its just getting (or in this case keeping) a deviant perception of reality. Mages in Quiet are in a similar situation. They are intentionally or unintentionally changing the reality that reaches them. They see clearly, they are just looking at the wrong thing; a magically induced echo chamber.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T17:51:53-07:00","id":1564105,"title":"","content":"That is indeed a good example.<br /> <br /> One exercise I like is to follow how Jhor is so widespread in the Chakravanti:<br /> <br /> Euthanatos paradigm defends that the Wheel must turn for the good of all, and their primary role as its keepers is as healers. Death is not a primary goal, it's for lost causes, ideally select with high criteria.<br /> <br /> Mastery of Entropy means their simplest tool to judge this criteria is Magic to look a person's place in the Wheel more or less directly. That means they cast Magic to judge fate and future morals in the worse cases possible, young and healthy bastards. They don't need to do it with people they think that can get better, only with those that may be lost causes.<br /> <br /> Rince and repeat Magic used in horrible people to see if their path has any chance at improving with the occasional &quot;no&quot; weighing heavier by the day.<br /> <br /> Forget how that affect a person's outlook. This changes Resonance. It gathers the desperation of the Mage when forced into this analysis, it gathers the symbolic weight of the bad results, much heavier than the good-ish ones. Captures whatever the target did in the past to be under scrutiny this heavy, and may do yet if trends are followed. The feelings of sorrow and anger the Mage must feel either toward the target, their victims or themselves. The Magic is changing.<br /> <br /> A Mage can dive into their demons for a series of reasons, and they may find solace and heal the marks, that's whatever comes afterward. But Resonance reacts to Magic, especially if it is important, and their wholesome moments aren't probably when their greatest Magic work is performed. The Magic remembers that bad place keener than the Mage.<br /> <br /> Low key Jhor is probably the Magic responding in accordance to accrued Resonance. Results get darker. Readings emphasize the bad stuff and mute the good. It's initially superficial, but little by little the Magic itself leans towards the worse judgment for people who would get a pass before.<br /> <br /> Rinse and repeat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T18:11:16-07:00","id":1564106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564024-charms-for-warding-against-quiet?p=1564071#post1564071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not exactly, but that's beyond the scope here. What they asked for was a charm to help against it, not a seal to eliminate it.<br /> <br /> And neither the Quiet or the personal growth come from the Avatar. We don't know where any of them come from or the nature of their relationship, but we do know Mages existed before Avatars as we understand them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Operative phrase: \u201cas we understand them.\u201d Dark Ages: Mage made the observation that in that era, mages doing have Avatars in the modern sense because whatever it is that assigns Avatars to mages was doing such an excellent job of pairing them up in that era that the Avatars never felt a need to guide their mortal companions; so they remained basically silent even after Awakening. There were still technically Avatars; but the Avatar Background was replaced by a Fount(?) Background that included all of Avatar's technical benefits without any of the \u201cvoice in your head\u201d aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T20:28:59-07:00","id":1564111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564024-charms-for-warding-against-quiet?p=1564106#post1564106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Operative phrase: \u201cas we understand them.\u201d Dark Ages: Mage made the observation that in that era, mages doing have Avatars in the modern sense because whatever it is that assigns Avatars to mages was doing such an excellent job of pairing them up in that era that the Avatars never felt a need to guide their mortal companions; so they remained basically silent even after Awakening. There were still technically Avatars; but the Avatar Background was replaced by a Fount(?) Background that included all of Avatar's technical benefits without any of the \u201cvoice in your head\u201d aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> But with the changes in lore that Avatars went through, we can't say anything about how far back it went.<br /> <br /> The point being, to say the growth of a Mage comes from the Avatar is either inaccurate or bold, as it has too many caveats to give any certainty. I mean, even more than usual.<br /> <br /> Now, saying Avatars <i>guide</i> their Mage is, as far as we know, correct, but guidance and source are not the same.<br /> <br /> Either way, the game is careful to never state that the Avatar has to have any participation in either enhancing Arete or achieving Ascension. It has a drive to be there, but the reason is in the pile of &quot;we don't know hard&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T12:49:15-07:00","id":1564248,"title":"","content":"I'd put it in the box of 'mage issues' same as paradox. You can't use magic to deal with it and if you can it's limited and tricky.<br /> <br /> Like getting a familiar to eat some paradox, it can't eat all of it and you have to care for it and it's more than just a spell <br /> <br /> You shouldn't need much of mind to ward against mundane derangements, so if you wanted to deal with it with magic start there and add some extra steps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T04:30:32-07:00","id":1564348,"title":"","content":"Hi there, thanks for the replies. I see now that HDYDT didn't help at all. <br /> <br /> What I first had in mind was pretty simple: a character with, for example, frequent intrusive thoughts, anxiety, insecurities, etc., could make a charm to deal with these issues by giving the Mage a metaphysical &quot;pat on the back&quot; by way of simply alerting said Mage (If the charm could talk and it would likely say just &quot;You are overthinking, my friend&quot;, or something like that). This idea is similar to what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> suggested with a charm to alert when you are in Quiet. Mechanically, I thought it would be pretty simple and give some flavor to the character, some level 1 spheres and the like, maybe the effect being just a free Willpower for the scene or something like that.<br /> <br /> And then... I read HDYDT... (maybe I got some Quiet from the experience).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28986-agrat","name":"Agrat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28986_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T05:04:06-07:00","id":1564352,"title":"","content":"A character with diagnosed anxiety manifesting intrusive thoughts only needs Mind 1 and a basic success. It won't cure the anxiety, but giving the equivalent of 1 WP to deal with it seems right. The voice doesn't even require an extra success, seriously.<br /> <br /> That book causes Aggravated damage to the brain, be more careful handling it, stay safe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}